ld be ok for something like this.\r\nI guess I was reinventing the wheel here XD"],"path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","id":37814,"created_at":"2024-10-10T13:40:50Z","original_position":27,"side":"RIGHT","position":28,"submitted_on_commit":"b3afc14824b2494dc26f4a7b7fe9967058d04c61","diff_hunk":"@@ -32,14 +36,75 @@ public TDigestStateReleasingTests(TDigestState.Type digestType) {\n         this.digestType \u003d digestType;\n     }\n \n+    public void testCreateOfType() {\n+        testCircuitBreakerTrip(circuitBreaker -\u003e TDigestState.createOfType(circuitBreaker, digestType, 100));\n+    }\n+\n+    public void testCreateUsingParamsFrom() {\n+        testCircuitBreakerTrip(circuitBreaker -\u003e {\n+            try (TDigestState example \u003d TDigestState.createOfType(newLimitedBreaker(ByteSizeValue.ofMb(100)), digestType, 100)) {\n+                return TDigestState.createUsingParamsFrom(example);\n+            }\n+        });","submitted_line":48},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"Similar to `#HTDZP`, the test method `testCreateUsingParamsFrom` could benefit from additional comments explaining its intent and expected behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java--1646:1968","promptId":"#6C9E4","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/TDigestStateReleasingTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1646,"endPos":1968,"startLine":43,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":5,"length":323}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":8,"uncoveredMatchable":1,"timing":29702,"tokensIn":6353,"tokensOut":677}